#: src/themes.md:3
msgid "Themes"
msgstr "主題"

#: src/themes.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed comes with a number of built-in themes, with more themes available as "
"extensions."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:7
msgid "Selecting a Theme"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:9
msgid ""
"See what themes are installed and preview them via the Theme Selector, which "
"you can open from the command palette with the `theme selector: toggle` "
"(bound to <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-k cmd-t|ctrl-k ctrl-t</kbd>) action."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:11
msgid ""
"Navigating through the theme list by moving up and down will change the "
"theme in real time and hitting enter will save the selected one to your "
"settings file."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:13
msgid "Installing New Themes"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:15
msgid ""
"You can find hundreds of different theme options in Zed's extensions store, "
"which you can access via the command palette with `zed: extensions` or the "
"[Zed website](https://zed.dev/extensions?filter=themes)."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:17
msgid ""
"Many popular themes have been ported to Zed, and if you're struggling to "
"choose one, visit [zed-themes.com](https://zed-themes.com), a third-party "
"gallery with visible previews for many of them."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:19
msgid "Build Your Theme"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:21
msgid ""
"You can use [Zed's Theme Builder](https://zed.dev/theme-builder) to design "
"your own custom theme based on an existing one."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:23
msgid ""
"This tool lets you fine-tune and preview how every surface in the Zed app "
"will look. You can then export the JSON for [local use](./themes.md#local-"
"themes) or for [publishing in Zed's extension store](./extensions/themes.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:26
msgid "Configuring a Theme"
msgstr "組態主題"

#: src/themes.md:28
msgid ""
"Your selected theme is stored in your settings file. You can open your "
"settings file from the command palette with <code class=\"hljs\">zed: open "
"settings file</code> (bound to <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-,|ctrl-alt-,"
"</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:31
msgid ""
"By default, Zed maintains two themes: one for light mode and one for dark "
"mode. You can set the mode to `\"dark\"` or `\"light\"` to ignore the "
"current system mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:36 src/themes.md:52 src/themes.md:60
msgid "\"theme\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:37 src/themes.md:61
msgid "\"mode\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:37 src/themes.md:61
msgid "\"system\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:38 src/themes.md:62
msgid "\"light\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:38 src/themes.md:62
msgid "\"One Light\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:39 src/themes.md:63
msgid "\"dark\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:39 src/themes.md:63 src/themes.md:83
msgid "\"One Dark\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:44
msgid "Toggle Theme Mode from the Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:46
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-k cmd-shift-t|ctrl-k ctrl-shift-t</kbd> to "
"switch the current theme mode between light and dark."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:48
msgid "If your settings currently use a static theme value, like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:52
msgid "\"Any Theme\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:56
msgid ""
"the first toggle converts it to dynamic theme selection with default themes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:68
msgid ""
"You are required to set both `light` and `dark` themes manually after the "
"first toggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:70
msgid ""
"After that, toggling updates only `theme.mode`. If `light` and `dark` are "
"the same theme, the first toggle may not produce a visible UI change until "
"you set different values for `light` and `dark`."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:73
msgid "Theme Overrides"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:75
msgid ""
"To override specific attributes of a theme, use the `theme_overrides` "
"setting. This setting can be used to configure theme-specific overrides."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:78
msgid ""
"For example, add the following to your `settings.json` if you wish to "
"override the background color of the editor and display comments and doc "
"comments as italics:"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:82
msgid "\"theme_overrides\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:84
msgid "\"editor.background\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:84
msgid "\"#333\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:85
msgid "\"syntax\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:86
msgid "\"comment\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:87 src/themes.md:90
msgid "\"font_style\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:87 src/themes.md:90
msgid "\"italic\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:89
msgid "\"comment.doc\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:93
msgid "\"accents\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:94
msgid "\"#ff0000\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:95
msgid "\"#ff7f00\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:96
msgid "\"#ffff00\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:97
msgid "\"#00ff00\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:98
msgid "\"#0000ff\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:99
msgid "\"#8b00ff\""
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:106
msgid ""
"To see a comprehensive list of list of captures (like `comment` and `comment."
"doc`) see [Language Extensions: Syntax highlighting](./extensions/languages."
"md#syntax-highlighting)."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:108
msgid ""
"To see a list of available theme attributes look at the JSON file for your "
"theme. For example, [assets/themes/one/one.json](https://github.com/zed-"
"industries/zed/blob/main/assets/themes/one/one.json) for the default One "
"Dark and One Light themes."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:111
msgid "Local Themes"
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:113
msgid ""
"Store new themes locally by placing them in the `~/.config/zed/themes` "
"directory (macOS and Linux) or `%USERPROFILE%"
"\\AppData\\Roaming\\Zed\\themes\\` (Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: src/themes.md:115
msgid ""
"For example, to create a new theme called `my-cool-theme`, create a file "
"called `my-cool-theme.json` in that directory. It will be available in the "
"theme selector the next time Zed loads."
msgstr ""
